  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Lupkynis (voclosporin), Version 1; Original: 7/7/2021; Approval: 09/17/21; Effective: 11/1/21. PDL status unknown: source is silent.",
    "Closed indication: active lupus nephritis. Biopsy must show active ISN/RPS Class III or IV, alone or with Class V; pure Class V does not meet approval criterion 3a. Criterion 3b states UPCR \u22651.5 mg/mg for Class III or IV OR \u22652 mg/mg for Class V. This encoding applies the Class V threshold to mixed III/IV + V; the source does not explicitly resolve overlapping classes and borderline mixed-class cases require manual review.",
    "Failure to meet approval criteria and every explicit denial exclusion are encoded. Blood pressure >165/105 is interpreted as either systolic >165 or diastolic >105; equality at both limits is allowed. eGFR must be strictly greater than 45. Lab submission and safety thresholds are attestations, not independently verified records.",
    "Monitoring (notes only): assess eGFR every two weeks for the first month and every four weeks thereafter.",
    "Duration (manual review): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 6 months if the prescriber documents disease improvement and/or stabilization OR improvement in the slope of decline.",
    "Quantity limit: 180 capsules per 30 days; enforcement requires manual review.",
    "Cautions (notes only): monitor closely for nephrotoxicity and neurotoxicity. Hypertension may require antihypertensive therapy. Consider electrocardiograms and electrolyte monitoring in high-risk patients. Avoid live vaccines during therapy.",
    "Benlysta is linked as an LN peer, not a combination recommendation or automatic substitution; its separate indication and eligibility facts must be evaluated. Benlysta criteria prohibit concomitant Lupkynis.",
    "Remaining gaps: evidence verification, mixed-class UPCR interpretation, monitoring schedule, duration, reauthorization response, quantity enforcement and cautions require manual review."
  ],
